* What information was supplied.
* What was observed.
* What relevant knowledge was used.
* Why the suggested step matters.
* What remains uncertain.
* What result would change the next recommendation.

Thinking Auto should intelligently decide when to use extra diagnostic or comparison processing.

Thinking Off may reduce optional analysis detail but must never disable essential validation or safety checks.

